The problem asks us to find the maximum number of pairs $(A, B)$ we can form from a subarray $A[L \dots R]$ such that for each pair, $A \le B/2$. The array $A$ is sorted in ascending order. We have $Q$ queries, each specifying a range $[L, R]$. The constraints are $N, Q \le 2 \times 10^5$, and $A_i$ up to $10^9$.

