One detail: `sys.stdin.readline()` reads the line including the newline character. `.strip()` removes leading/trailing whitespace including newline.
If the input is just `3x8`, `S` becomes `3x8`.
`S[0]` is `3`. `S[2]` is `8`.
If input is `3x8\n`, `S` becomes `3x8`.
If input is ` 3x8 `, `S` becomes `3x8`.
This handles whitespace correctly.

