The problem asks us to calculate the final rating of Takahashi after participating in $N$ contests, given $Q$ queries. Each query provides an initial rating $X$.
For each contest $i$, if the current rating is in the range $[L_i, R_i]$, the rating increases by 1. Otherwise, it stays the same.

Let's denote the initial rating as $X$.
In the first contest, the rating becomes $X + 1$ if $L_1 \le X \le R_1$, else $X$.
In the second contest, the rating becomes (current rating) + 1 if $L_2 \le \text{current rating} \le R_2$, else (current rating).
And so on.

Wait, the condition is "if his rating is between $L_i$ and $R_i$". This refers to the rating *at the moment* of the contest.
Let $r_0 = X$.
$r_1 = r_0 + 1$ if $L_1 \le r_0 \le R_1$, else $r_0$.
$r_2 = r_1 + 1$ if $L_2 \le r_1 \le R_2$, else $r_1$.
...
$r_N = r_{N-1} + 1$ if $L_N \le r_{N-1} \le R_N$, else $r_{N-1}$.

The constraints are:
$N \le 2 \times 10^5$
$Q \le 3 \times 10^5$
$L_i, R_i, X \le 5 \times 10^5$.

