$r_0 = X$.
$r_1 = X + \mathbb{I}(L_1 \le X \le R_1)$.
$r_2 = r_1 + \mathbb{I}(L_2 \le r_1 \le R_2) = X + \mathbb{I}(L_1 \le X \le R_1) + \mathbb{I}(L_2 \le r_1 \le R_2)$.
Notice that $r_1$ depends on $X$. Specifically, $r_1$ is either $X$ or $X+1$.
