If $L_2 \le X \le R_2$, then if $r_1=X$, it increases. If $r_1=X+1$, it might or might not.
If $X+1 \le L_2$ or $X+1 > R_2$, then $r_1=X+1$ doesn't increase.
If $L_2 \le X+1 \le R_2$, then $r_1=X+1$ increases.

